## The graph's own reasoning channels

`hard_negatives.json`, under the registered publication-disjoint protocol on
the plate-matched population.

{{hn_table}}

Read the `floor` and `skill` columns before the AUC.
{{hn_n_channels_clearing}} of the {{hn_n_channels}} metapath channels has an
interval excluding {{chance}} ({{hn_channels_clearing}}). The two scorers that
do are the ensemble ({{hn_combined_auc}} {{hn_combined_ci}}, skill
{{hn_combined_skill}}) and the **degree baseline** ({{hn_degree_auc}}
{{hn_degree_ci}}, skill {{hn_degree_skill}}) — and the difference between them
is the floor, not the AUC: degree reaches {{hn_degree_cov}} of the positives so
its floor is exactly {{chance}} and all of its margin is ranking, while the
ensemble reaches {{hn_combined_cov}} and its coverage asymmetry **alone** scores
{{hn_combined_floor}}.

`metapath_comparison.json` covers {{mc_n_viruses}} viruses and the channels
{{mc_channels}}. With the correction family fixed in advance, the survivors
are:

{{correction_table}}

